    With the driver cache disabled the numbers are reproducible: a 535,936 byte
    runtime-cache file turns a 663 ms first inference into 39 ms.
    With it enabled the cold number is whatever the shared on-disk cache happens to hold
    (155 to 654 ms across repeated runs here), so the ratio moves between ~7x and ~28x
    without anything about TensorRT changing. The warm number is stable either way --
    that is the one to quote. A server that restarts without shipping this file pays the
    compile again, and cannot rely on the driver cache to hide it.
